"""The motion skills a request plans with: ``walk`` (``skills.walk``, generated by ``skills.walking``) and ``hold``.

A skill is a function ``(start: StartState, params) -> MotionDraft`` with a frozen dataclass of parameters
(``core.params``). It always starts at the origin facing +x: ``planner.steps.run_skill`` moves it into the step's own
frame, maps its result back, keeps the arms at their joint angles and stages the default limits; the planner checks the
whole motion. ``frames[0]`` is the start pose. A skill refuses only what it cannot build a motion from: INVALID_REQUEST
(its parameters), PRECONDITION (its start) or, for ``walk``, PLAN_REJECTED (the walker's own refusals: a start stance
or height it does not walk from, or attempts that failed its checks).
"""
